HighInBC wrote:
[much snippage]
> Will my helmet defend me against the flayers attack?? I have no insta
> kill methods like /oDeath or +FOD. Any trick to getting a titan? both
> are sleep resist. I don't want to proceed until I have a better idea of
> what to do.

A helmet has a probability of protecting you, but given the number of
attacks a mindflayer has  I would expect to lose at least 4 points of
Int in melee with a mind flayer.

A greased helmet will ... as far as I know -- offer complete protection
as long as the grease holds out, which would probably be about 6
attacks. Then the attacks start getting through.

There is no good way to melee mindflayers.

Here's some thoughts, in order of increasing risk:

1) Consider collecting ordinary missile weapons and use them to kill
the mindflayer. Monk is restricted in all but crossbow,  but if you
have enough of them you can make up for the penalties.   If you do
this, make sure you have a way to escape if things get tough.

2) Find some tripe in Sokoban or the mines and use it to tame a dog/cat
or two. Then take him down to the Gnome Mines polytrap and see if you
can't get a decent pet out of him.  Then let your pet deal with one of
the monsters while you kill the other.

3) You have a wand of teleport ... use it when fighting the two
creatures.  Concentrate on one, and when the other gets too close, use
the wand of teleport to send him to the far side of the dungeon.  By
the time he gets back, you'll have killed your first quarry and be
ready for the second.

3)  Consider finding someone with a still functioning wand of digging
and, er, "acquiring" it.  If you're SURE it has charges left,  use it
to engrave Elbereth in 1 turn. Then you can smack around both the MMF
and the Titan with impunity .. or until the E gets smudged, which
should take a few turns.   Check at the beginning of every turn to see
if it has become smudged.  If it has, re-engrave and continue your
beat-down.  If you're out of charges, run away. I don't think you'll
need more than two.

A wand of fire is even better, because E burned with fire NEVER (as far
as I know) gets smudged, so you have a permanent safe square.

4)  If you're really desperate, consider going back to the Gnomish
mines and getting yourself a pickaxe. Then go straight through the
floor on that level and bypass the Titan and MMF altogether. Come back
up when you've acquired  the necessary equipment to demolish them.


I have never completed the Monk Quest, so I can't give specific advice
there. I have heard, however, that it is one of the hardest quests in
Nethack, and is often left until after the Castle is cleared.

